"comparison": "Both Nvidia and AMD disclose risks related to their dependency on third-party entities for critical components of their product ecosystems and development capabilities. Nvidia specifically relies on third-party developers and content providers to build applications and make content available on its platforms (e.g., GeForce NOW), noting that failure by these parties could adversely affect customer demand. Similarly, AMD relies on third-party intellectual property, including development and testing tools, as well as acquired features, to design and introduce new products. AMD highlights that if this third-party IP becomes unavailable, fails to meet performance requirements, or is restricted by law, its business could be materially adversely affected. While Nvidia's risk centers on the software/content ecosystem and customer demand, AMD's risk focuses on the hardware/software design inputs, both constituting a fundamental dependency on external third-party contributions to their core business offerings.",
